\f4\fs26 \'93What happened with the Commissioner?\'94 Sarah decided to start off feigning interest in Hayley\'92s meeting with her boss.\
\'93Detective Chief Superintendent,\'94 she announced proudly, letting out an adolescent giggle. \'93I am in charge of all criminal investigations across the entire dominion.\'94\
\'93Did what did he say?\'94\
\'93What could he say? The contract on Cracker was open for anyone. He could do nothing but what he promised or lose the support of the rank and file.\'94 Hayley knew the Commissioner would be gunning for her now. \'93I will have to fly under the radar for a while, though.\'94\
\'93Hayley I really need some female advice.\'94 \
\'93You mean real advice?\'94 Hayley chuckled.\
\'93They don\'92t have a clue about important issues.\'94 She looked at the tribe inside the private box. \'93You know about the clone, right? But you know it was deposited inside me without consent.\'94\
\'93You were raped? Get rid of it.\'94 Hayley shot back. \'93I will happily charge anyone involved.\'94\
\'93It is not quite that easy. You see all the Elvi here? They believe I am carrying their Saviour. You may have heard about him, the Elvi call him the one-after-the-one.\'94\
\'93I heard something along those lines, but didn\'92t give it much credence. I mean, it seems more than a little absurd. I have seen the posters everywhere, \'91The one-after-the-one is coming\'92, but I thought it was all some sort of advertising campaign. So why can\'92t you abort?\'94 \
\'93The Elvi are all adolescents and they will go berserk if I terminate. There\'92s 100,000 of them. Can you imagine the carnage? I will most certainly be hunted down and killed, along with Cracker.\'94\
\'93Okay then, don\'92t terminate.\'94 \
\'93There is another problem. Do you remember what Dr Logan told us at the morgue?\'94\
\'93Yes, but I didn\'92t take it all in, I was still in a bit of shock. With you shooting Cracker and then his remarkable recovery.\'94\
\'93Don\'92t ask how, but there is synthetic DNA attached to the child\'92s DNA and I don\'92t know what he will turn out like. He could be hideous.\'94 Sarah scrunched her face up and looked away.\
\'93I see your dilemma.\'94 Hayley said calmly. 
\f5\i Holy tax fraud! What a mess!
\f4\i0 \
\'93What will happen if I have him?\'94\
\'93Are you sure it\'92s a him?\'94\
\'93Yes, the clone will be the same sex as the original.\'94 \
\'93Then I would not worry about the child being hideous. All men are.\'94 Hayley quipped and Sarah laughed.\
\'93So true, so true.\'94 It was the first time Sarah had laughed since Kathy had told her the news. \
\'93When they\'92re not trying to fuck you or kill you, men are really funny.\'94 Hayley was momentarily deadpan before both busted out giggling. \'93Men do create problems, but in this situation they, or at least one of them, may be the solution. You must realise the difficulties of raising a child as a single mother. Apart from the obvious problem of doing all the work yourself, you will find discrimination from your boss and disdain from your colleagues, male and female alike. No-one in authority will ever say out loud that you are not wanted, but you will see evidence of it piling up everyday. The treatment of management-level single mothers is unconscionable - upper management does not like square pegs. All their talk about diversity is just that, talk.\'94 Hayley had seen it over and over again. \
\'93Treating mothers like that is disgraceful and just plain moronic.\'94 Over many years, Sarah just like Hayley, had seen the terrible abuse single mothers received at the hands of a patriarchal zeitgeist.\
\'93Don\'92t think it is an operation of puritanical morality. It is nothing of the sort. It is a feeding frenzy of the strong destroying the weak, utterly. Like chickens pecking to death the weakest of their number, you will be identified as vulnerable and your workmates will be compelled to humiliate and punish. Senior executives want, no, they demand compliance. It is contemptible but allocation will fix all of this. Just make sure you specify level 5 and above. You don\'92t want to allocate beneath your station.\'94 Hayley pointed to Cracker who doing a maniacal-macarana with Kathy.\
\'93Allocation? It\'92s not something that I had ever contemplated. I have always regarded marriage-at-random a sign of desperation.\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
\'93Termination or allocation. I think they weigh about the same. I still have some thinking to do, Hayley.\'94\
\'91Not too long I hope. You are not showing at the moment, so you might be able to pass the child off as his, although you would have to get someone pretty stupid though.\'94\
\'93A stupid level 5? Not likely.\'94
